      "voiceover_script": "The product life cycle shows the stages a product passes through: introduction, growth, maturity and decline. A curve draws in. Sales climb from two thousand units in introduction, to nine thousand in growth, to fourteen thousand at maturity, then ease to six thousand in decline. The line rises, flattens, then falls. Each stage needs a different mix: launch spending early, differentiation at maturity, cost control late. Reading the curve tells managers when to act.",
